PLACEHOLDER MODEL FILE - NOT A VALID TFLITE FLATBUFFER.

The app intentionally ships this placeholder so the project builds and runs before
any model exists. On load, react-native-fast-tflite will throw, and the app shows
a friendly 'model missing' state while the rest of the flow stays testable.

To replace it with a valid (but random-weights) model:
    cd model_training && pip install -r requirements.txt && python make_dummy_model.py

After real training + conversion:
    python convert_tflite.py   # overwrites this file with the trained float16 model

DO NOT edit this file by hand.
